# CoreLink — public-base-allowlist (F3.2 increment 3: the digest-pinned,
# owner-gated trust root that governs which upstream layers may EVER reside in
# the cross-tenant `_public` cache).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY THIS FILE IS THE TRUST ROOT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The `_public` namespace dedups content-addressed blobs across EVERY tenant. A
# poisoned or misclassified blob that enters `_public` serves cross-tenant. So
# the set of digests eligible for `_public` is a security boundary. This file is
# that boundary, and it is deliberately the most owner-gated artifact we have:
#
#   * BAKED INTO THE CONTAINER at build time (`include_str!`). There is NO runtime
#     mutation path — no API, no D1 write, no admin endpoint can widen it. The
#     ONLY way to add or remove an entry is a reviewed code commit + a redeploy.
#     A compromised token or a D1 write therefore cannot enlarge what may enter
#     `_public`. (design Contradiction-2: allowlist commits are out-of-band /
#     owner-gated, never runtime-mutable.)
#
#   * DIGEST-PINNED, NEVER TAG-RESOLVED. Every active entry is an immutable
#     upstream OCI content digest `sha256:<64 lowercase hex>`. TAGS ARE BANNED:
#     a tag (`ubuntu:22.04`) is mutable and re-resolving it is exactly the
#     poisoning vector content-addressing closes (design BLOCKER-3). The loader
#     (`public_base_allowlist.rs`) FAIL-CLOSES on any non-digest active line —
#     one bad entry makes the whole load error, so the public-base router refuses
#     to arm rather than trust a partially-valid allowlist.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW AN ENTRY IS ADDED (the owner-gated, populate-then-allowlist procedure)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ORDERING INVARIANT (design GAP-E): a digest may be added here ONLY AFTER the
# server's own trusted mirror has already populated `_public` for it (the
# increment-4 SSRF-safe server-only mirror job). Allowlisting a digest the server
# has NOT yet mirrored would let a CLIENT push be the one that populates the
# shared blob — the exact hole this control closes. So the procedure is:
#   1. Owner pins an upstream base layer OUT OF BAND: resolve `repo:tag` to its
#      immutable `sha256:` layer digest yourself (e.g. `docker buildx imagetools
#      inspect`), and record the pin below with provenance.
#   2. The increment-4 mirror job pulls THAT pinned digest through the trusted
#      registry path, verifies the bytes, and populates `_public`.
#   3. ONLY THEN is the digest un-commented here and shipped in a redeploy.
# Revocation of a compromised base is the B1b `_public` blocklist kill-switch
# (`/_internal/public/revoke`) — orthogonal to this file.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FORMAT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   sha256:<64 lowercase hex>    <provenance: registry/repo:tag (arch) it was pinned from>
# `#` starts a comment (whole-line or trailing). Blank lines ignored. Only the
# leading whitespace-delimited token per active line is parsed; the rest is
# human provenance.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ACTIVE ALLOWLIST — WP-G M3: alpine layer (WP-E) + 5 base IMAGE index digests.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWO KINDS of entry now coexist, both digest-pinned + owner-gated:
#
#  1. LAYER-blob digest (WP-E model). A single upstream rootfs LAYER blob. Gates
#     BOTH the client-push `_public` route (`finalize_upload` `routes_to_public`)
#     and the server mirror (`/_internal/admin/public-mirror/promote`). The alpine
#     amd64 rootfs layer below is the one such pin.
#
#  2. base-image INDEX/manifest digest (WP-G M2 model). An immutable multi-arch
#     INDEX (or image-manifest) digest. On the FIRST request for
#     `<repo>@sha256:<index>` under both flags ON, the M2 resolver
#     (`promote_public_closure`, `routes/public_pullthrough.rs`) fetches the
#     closure from the FIXED upstream (`registry-1.docker.io`), digest-verifies
#     EVERY descriptor (index → linux per-arch children → config + layers)
#     fail-CLOSED, and promotes the whole closure into `_public`; later tenants
#     serve it cross-tenant by EXISTENCE. This SUPERSEDES GAP-E's separate
#     "mirror-populates-first" step: the on-demand promote IS the trusted server
#     populate, and it is fused with the read. It opens NO client-push hole —
#     client pushes route by LAYER digest and these index digests are NOT layer
#     digests, so a client can never populate `_public` for them; only the
#     server-side, upstream-verified closure promote can.
#
# ACTIVATION (M3): both `OCI_PUBLIC_DEDUP_ENABLED` and `OCI_UPSTREAM_ON_MISS` are
# "1" in prod (baked-boot flags; activation is a repin). Revocation of any
# promoted digest is the B1b `_public` blocklist kill-switch
# (`/_internal/public/revoke`) — orthogonal to this file.
#
# NOTE (drift): index digests are the CURRENT resolution of a mutable tag; a base
# rebuild yields a NEW index digest. A stale pin still serves whoever requests
# that exact digest (content-addressed); refresh = owner re-pins out of band.
#
# ── LAYER pins (WP-E) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sha256:25f1d6b1951ac8eb3740558fe94cb83d377bdadf95fd9f98b50d2e1b96130471   docker.io/library/alpine:3.20 (amd64 rootfs layer)
#
# ── base-image INDEX pins (WP-G M2), resolved 2026-08-19 ──────────────────────
sha256:d9e853e87e55526f6b2917df91a2115c36dd7c696a35be12163d44e6e2a4b6bc   docker.io/library/alpine:3.20 (multi-arch image index)
sha256:813017f3d62be4b5891a7acca6a01bdcd4b8513daa81b1ab99d3a50385b26931   docker.io/library/debian:12 (multi-arch image index)
sha256:33ceb71981b602c1a7443a53469e4dba065f7503eab3078a2d7a57a2ab987517   docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04 (multi-arch image index)
sha256:d649c27dae7ba0137b3cef5dd75baa422c08dc3d9e3fc0c23dfb172dc3cc6436   docker.io/library/node:22-slim (multi-arch image index)
sha256:2c941e860699f878900b0edc2403613c234d4b32eda3cc9fa7036991a2a63c4a   docker.io/library/python:3.12-slim (multi-arch image index)
